					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5188</guid>
				<title>SCP-5188</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5188</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Item #:** SCP5188&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; keter&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5188 is a pit approximately 29km in width and length however it increases by 10 meter each day. It is located in a deselet area of Russia but also12km away from the town of Irkutsk. It was discovered in 2003 when people on a plane saw the pit when looking out there windows at wich point the Russian government sent a squad of 7 soldiers to investigate the pit. There were 4 males and 3 females. They each had a standard Russian army uniform and a 97 watt light with them. Only 1 member escaped due to unknown circumstances. No trace of them was ever found again. At that point the Russian government called for foundation units to investigate the pit and try to secure it. An MTF squadron, each equipped with a standard MTF uniform, a 120 watt light, a camera, and the leader had a communication device to scientist back at the site. During the first minutes one of the MTF squadron members discover that it was slowly increasing in its length and width. The site then instructed the squadron to make a campsite near it, with resources on there way. When they arrived they did so and made a base called [DATA REDACTED]. At some point that day a member of the squadron decided to go into the pit, which was accept by the leader, as he descend down the pit his Camara deactivated. The other members projected there light down the pit and could not see him. After 11 minutes of the member not exiting the leader called a full retreat. This operation has been logged by the foundation in the foundations files. One more operation was carried out via drone. Once the drone was lowered into the pit it went on longer than nature would allow. The drone went on, descending into the pit for for 1 hour and 37 minutes and went down a total of 173km befor it ran out of battery, during this no end was recordedly found. 1 month later D-class testing was approved and began on the same day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/that1writer&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7032233&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1609943758&quot; alt=&quot;That1writer &quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7032233)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/that1writer&quot;  &gt;That1writer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
