f the legs, which capture them and carry them into the large central mouth for envenomation and consumption. Preys primarily on other black-widow- and scorpion-type SCP-2199-1 instances.</td> </tr> </table> </blockquote> <p>SCP-2199 was discovered outside of Cairo, Egypt in an abandoned desert ruin, with two near-human skeletons. In addition, the ancient remains of several other animals were discovered. The identified specimens include a horse, crocodile, abnormally large birds, and whale bones. The following script was found etched into the wall, translated from Latin.</p> <blockquote> <p><em>The carrier/holder/ark has crashed, and we are truly lost/alone. There is nobody to inherit/take the last guardians/warlords of life, and they will be lost in time. This development is unfortunate, but inevitable/destined. They probably wouldn't have gotten along in this dead place.</em></p> </blockquote> <p>Since the discovery of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3150">SCP-3150</a> in 194█, no less than two similar entities to SCP-2199 have have been observed within SCP-3150-1. Investigation into SCP-2199's origins via SCP-3150-3 is currently pending review.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-96806-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. This is despite SCP-2199 containing normal internal organs</div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2198">SCP-2198</a> | SCP-2199 | <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2200">SCP-2200</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1229263&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609943761" alt="RJB_R" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1229263)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r" >RJB_R</a></span></p> 
